                <div class="col-md-6 right-col">
                    <div class="faqs">
                        <div id="accordions" class="accordion">
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse1"><span><strong>Q1:</strong> What types of book illustrations do you offer (children's books, comics, educational, etc.)?</span></div></div><div id="collapse1" class="collapse show"><div class="card-body text"><p>We illustrate across every major category, children's picture books, early readers, middle grade titles, comic books, graphic novels, manga, educational textbooks, how-to guides, science and medical publications, cookbooks, and adult non-fiction requiring diagrams, maps, or decorative artwork. Each category involves different artistic requirements and different illustrator skill sets, and we match every project with an artist who works natively in that space rather than adapting a generic illustration approach.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse2"><span><strong>Q2:</strong> Do you create custom illustrations based on my story and characters?</span></div></div><div id="collapse2" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, every illustration we produce is original artwork created specifically for your book. Your characters are designed from scratch based on your descriptions and creative direction, your settings are illustrated to match the world you've built, and every scene is composed to serve the specific narrative moment it accompanies. We don't use pre-made assets, stock illustrations, or recycled artwork from other projects. Everything is custom, and everything is yours.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse3"><span><strong>Q3:</strong> What illustration styles are available (digital, watercolour, cartoon, realistic)?</span></div></div><div id="collapse3" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>We work across the full range of illustration styles, digital painting, traditional watercolour, pen and ink, cartoon and caricature, realistic and hyper-realistic, flat vector, mixed media, collage, retro, whimsical, and everything between. The right style depends on your genre, your audience, and the tone of your book. A playful watercolour approach suits many picture books. A clean digital style works well for educational content. A detailed realistic approach fits certain comics and graphic novels. We'll help you identify the best style for your project during your consultation.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse4"><span><strong>Q4:</strong> How does the illustration process work from concept to final artwork?</span></div></div><div id="collapse4" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>The process moves through five stages, creative brief, illustrator matching, character design and storyboarding, illustration production with ongoing review, and final file delivery. You're involved at every stage, giving feedback on sketches and works-in-progress before final artwork is produced. Nothing is finalised without your approval, and revisions are built into each phase so the finished illustrations match your vision for the book rather than surprising you at the end.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse5"><span><strong>Q5:</strong> How long does it take to complete book illustrations?</span></div></div><div id="collapse5" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Timelines depend on the number of illustrations, the complexity and style, and the format of your book. A standard thirty-two-page picture book with full-colour illustrations on every spread typically takes eight to twelve weeks from character design through final artwork delivery. Chapter books with spot illustrations take less time. Graphic novels and comics with high panel counts take considerably longer. We'll give you a clear, realistic timeline during your consultation based on your specific project scope.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse6"><span><strong>Q6:</strong> Do you provide character design and storyboard development?</span></div></div><div id="collapse6" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, both are included in our full illustration process and also available as standalone services. Character design produces detailed reference sheets, your characters from multiple angles, in various expressions, with costume and proportion details locked down before page illustration begins. Storyboarding maps out every spread or page with rough compositions showing text placement, visual flow, and narrative pacing. Both stages exist to resolve creative decisions before final artwork starts, saving time and preventing costly revisions later.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse7"><span><strong>Q7:</strong> Can illustrations be formatted for publishing platforms like Amazon KDP?</span></div></div><div id="collapse7" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We deliver final artwork in high-resolution files that meet the exact specifications of Amazon KDP, IngramSpark, Apple Books, and every other major publishing platform, correct colour profiles, resolution, bleed settings, and file formats for both print and digital distribution. For picture books and illustrated titles, we also handle the full layout assembly, integrating illustrations with text into finished, upload-ready book files that pass each platform's quality review without rejection.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse8"><span><strong>Q8:</strong> How much do book illustration services cost in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse8" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Illustration costs depend on the number of illustrations, the style and complexity, whether character design and storyboarding are included, and the format of your book. A picture book with sixteen full-spread illustrations costs more than a chapter book needing eight spot illustrations, and a graphic novel with hundreds of panels represents a larger project again. We quote individually based on your specific requirements, get in touch with your manuscript details and visual direction and we'll give you a clear, honest price built around what your book actually needs.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse9"><span><strong>Q9:</strong> Will I get revisions or changes during the illustration process?</span></div></div><div id="collapse9" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, revisions are included at every stage. You review character designs before page illustration begins, approve storyboard layouts before final artwork is produced, and give feedback on completed illustrations in batches as they're delivered. Colour adjustments, compositional changes, expression refinements, and other modifications are all part of the process. We work through revisions until each illustration meets your expectations, the goal is artwork you're proud to publish, not artwork you've settled for.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse10"><span><strong>Q10:</strong> Do you also offer layout and design along with illustrations?</span></div></div><div id="collapse10" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We offer complete book layout and design services alongside illustration, integrating your artwork with text, designing page compositions, and producing final files ready for print and digital publishing. For picture books and heavily illustrated titles, layout is particularly important because the relationship between text placement and illustration on each spread directly affects how the book reads. We handle the full production pipeline from original artwork through to a finished book file, so you don't need to coordinate between separate illustration and formatting providers.</p></div></div></div>
